WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.569 --> 00:00:22.476
The next day Adele and I had to vacate the library because Mr. Rochester wanted to use it as a reception room for callers.

2
00:00:22.477 --> 00:00:29.420
A fire was lit in an upstairs room, and there I carried our books and arranged it as a schoolroom.

3
00:00:29.421 --> 00:00:36.633
Thornfield was no longer as quiet as a church; every hour or two, it echoed with a knock at the door.

4
00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:41.893
Footsteps crossed the hall and new voices spoke in the rooms below.

5
00:00:41.894 --> 00:00:50.901
A stream from the outer world was flowing through Thornfield. The house had a master, and I liked it better that way.

6
00:00:50.902 --> 00:00:58.267
Adele was not easy to teach that day. She kept coming up with excuses to go downstairs.

7
00:00:58.268 --> 00:01:04.433
I suspected she was trying to visit the library, where I knew she wasn't wanted.

8
00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:13.617
When I made her sit still, she continued to prattle on about her friend, Mr. Edward Fairfax Rochester.

9
00:01:13.618 --> 00:01:24.438
That was the first time I'd heard his full name. Apparently he'd hinted to Adele that there would be a gift for her when his luggage arrived from Millcote.

10
00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:33.336
"Maybe there will be one for you too," she said to me in French. "Last night he was asking me about my governess."

11
00:01:33.337 --> 00:01:42.846
The afternoon was wild and snowy. When it grew dark, and there were no more guests, I allowed Adele to run downstairs.

12
00:01:42.847 --> 00:01:51.903
Left alone, I went to a window but could see nothing outside. I sat by the fire and stared at the embers.

13
00:01:51.904 --> 00:02:00.094
After a while Mrs. Fairfax came in and said that Mr. Rochester would like Adele and me to take tea with him.

14
00:02:00.095 --> 00:02:03.392
"Should I change my frock?" I asked.

15
00:02:03.393 --> 00:02:12.299
"Yes. I always dress up for the evening when he's here. You'll want to wear a brooch, if you have one."

16
00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:23.078
So I put on my black silk dress and a small pearl pin that Miss Temple had given me. I let Mrs. Fairfax precede me into the dining room.

17
00:02:23.079 --> 00:02:33.868
Adele was kneeling next to Pilot in front of the fireplace. Mr. Rochester was watching them as he lay on a couch, his foot supported by a pillow.

18
00:02:33.869 --> 00:02:39.867
I recognized my traveler with his black hair and eyebrows and his grim mouth.

19
00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:46.629
Without his traveling cloak, his figure appeared athletic, though neither tall nor graceful.

20
00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:51.864
He must have been aware of our entrance, but he appeared not to notice us.

21
00:02:51.865 --> 00:02:56.282
"Here is Miss Eyre, sir," said Mrs. Fairfax.

22
00:02:56.283 --> 00:03:01.588
He bowed his head, still not taking his eyes from Adele and Pilot.

23
00:03:01.589 --> 00:03:04.942
"Let Miss Eyre be seated," he said.

24
00:03:04.943 --> 00:03:14.768
There was something in the stiff, forced bow and his impatient yet formal tone that made me think he didn't care if I were there or not.

25
00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:20.084
If he'd treated me with excessive politeness, I might have been intimidated.

26
00:03:20.085 --> 00:03:25.836
But his manner was so eccentric that I was curious to see what he would do next.

27
00:03:25.837 --> 00:03:37.752
He behaved like a statue; that is, he neither spoke nor moved. Mrs. Fairfax began to make some polite conversation about his visitors and his injury.

28
00:03:37.753 --> 00:03:42.793
"Mrs. Fairfax, I would like some tea" was his only response.

29
00:03:42.794 --> 00:03:47.550
She rang for tea, and when it arrived, she asked me to pour it.

30
00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:55.978
As I handed a cup to Mr. Rochester, Adele cried out in French, "Do you have a gift for Miss Eyre in your luggage?"

31
00:03:55.979 --> 00:04:05.806
"What's this about gifts?" he responded gruffly in English. "Did you expect a gift, Miss Eyre? Are you fond of gifts?"

32
00:04:05.807 --> 00:04:13.291
"I hardly know, sir," I replied. "I have very little experience with them.

33
00:04:13.292 --> 00:04:17.955
But since I'm a stranger to you, I've done nothing to deserve a gift."

34
00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:26.281
"Oh, don't be so modest!" he scolded me. "I've quizzed Adele and find you've taken great pains with her.

35
00:04:26.282 --> 00:04:33.630
She's not bright and she has no talents. Yet in a short time, she has made great improvement."

36
00:04:33.631 --> 00:04:43.846
"Sir, you've now given me my gift. I'm obliged to you. The best gift for a teacher is praise for her student's progress."

37
00:04:43.847 --> 00:04:49.440
"Humph!" said Mr. Rochester, and he drank his tea in silence.

38
00:04:49.441 --> 00:04:59.936
When he had finished, he told me to come sit by the fire. Adele wanted to take a seat on my knee, but he ordered her to amuse herself with Pilot.

39
00:04:59.937 --> 00:05:06.329
He asked about my family and my life at Lowood. "I suppose you play the piano."

40
00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.493
"A little."

41
00:05:08.493 --> 00:05:18.486
"Of course. That's the expected answer. Go into the sitting room—I mean, please go into the sitting room and play a tune.

42
00:05:18.487 --> 00:05:25.144
I'm used to saying 'Do this,' and it's done. I can't change my habits for one new person."

43
00:05:25.145 --> 00:05:29.064
I went to the adjoining room to obey his instructions.

44
00:05:29.077 --> 00:05:38.401
"Enough!" he called out in a few minutes. "You play like any other English schoolgirl, perhaps better than some but not well."

45
00:05:38.402 --> 00:05:40.813
I returned to the dining room.

46
00:05:40.814 --> 00:05:46.564
"Adele showed me some of your sketches. Surely a drawing teacher helped you?"

47
00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:50.228
"No, indeed!" I said indignantly.

48
00:05:50.229 --> 00:05:58.133
"Ah, I've wounded your pride. Bring them here, and I'll determine whether they were done by one hand or two."

49
00:05:58.134 --> 00:06:04.293
I fetched my portfolio, and he went over my sketches and watercolors, which he seemed to like.

50
00:06:04.294 --> 00:06:10.787
He quizzed me: Was I happy while drawing? Was I satisfied with the results?

51
00:06:10.788 --> 00:06:15.334
Then he ordered me to take the pictures away and put Adele to bed.

52
00:06:15.335 --> 00:06:19.671
After I did that, I rejoined Mrs. Fairfax in her room.

53
00:06:19.672 --> 00:06:25.630
"Mr. Rochester is very abrupt and inconsistent," I observed.

54
00:06:25.631 --> 00:06:33.359
"No doubt he appears so to a stranger, but I'm used to him. We should make allowances for his temperament."

55
00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.931
"Why?"

56
00:06:34.932 --> 00:06:43.090
"Partly because it's his nature, and none of us can help our nature." Mrs. Fairfax picked up her knitting.

57
00:06:43.091 --> 00:06:47.994
"And partly because he has painful thoughts that harass him."

58
00:06:47.995 --> 00:06:50.060
"What kind of thoughts?"

59
00:06:50.061 --> 00:06:53.144
"Family troubles, for one thing."

60
00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:58.672
I was puzzled. "But he has no family."

61
00:06:58.672 --> 00:07:07.586
Mrs. Fairfax explained that Mr. Rochester's father had not wanted to divide his estate between Edward and his older brother, Rowland.

62
00:07:07.587 --> 00:07:13.315
But he also didn't want Edward to be impoverished when Rowland inherited everything.

63
00:07:13.316 --> 00:07:23.404
"Old Mr. Rochester and Rowland schemed to bring Edward into what Edward considered a painful situation for the sake of making his fortune.

64
00:07:23.405 --> 00:07:30.874
As a result, Edward broke with his family and shuns Thornfield," said Mrs. Fairfax.

65
00:07:30.875 --> 00:07:40.113
"After Rowland died nine years ago, Edward inherited Thornfield, but he seldom stays more than two weeks at a time."

66
00:07:40.114 --> 00:07:50.195
I didn't understand why my employer disliked Thornfield, but Mrs. Fairfax either could not or would not give me any more information.

67
00:07:50.196 --> 00:07:56.607
It was evident that she wanted me to drop the subject, and so I did.
